.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt CRONTAB 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm crontab
.Nd install, list or remove a per-user cron spool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l | Fl r
.Op Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility validates a five-field crontab and installs it atomically as
.Pa /var/cron/<user> .
With no file operand it reads standard input.
.Pp
The time fields are minute, hour, day of month, month and day of week.
Each accepts
.Ql * ,
a number, a range
.Pq Ql a-b ,
a comma list, and
.Ql /step .
The command must be non-empty.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l
List the current spool.
.It Fl r
Remove the current spool.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
does not interpret the command.
Shell metacharacters are supported only by a shell-capable
runner; the target crond executes a simple program plus arguments.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width CRON_SPOOL
.It Ev CRON_SPOOL
Override the spool directory.
Used by the host tests.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for a validation or spool error, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crond 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The five-field syntax, install/list/remove operations and atomic replacement follow POSIX
crontab. `@reboot` and GNU extensions are unsupported.
